   "text": {
    "L1": "When two straight lines cross, they make four angles at one meeting point.",
    "L2": "Angles next to each other on a straight line form a linear pair, so they add to 180 degrees.",
    "L3": "Vertically opposite means across the crossing point, not simply above and below.",
    "L4": "Across angles are equal because each makes a linear pair with the same neighbouring angle.",
    "L5": "If one angle is 72 degrees, its opposite is 72 degrees, and each neighbour is 180 minus 72, or 108 degrees.",
    "L6": "So the four angles are 72 degrees, 108 degrees, 72 degrees and 108 degrees.",
    "L7": "Now choose the angle vertically opposite to 72 degrees."
   },
